 "status_note": "Proposed content pending the owner's OI-MTQ-03 (scope rules) and OI-MTQ-04 (quantity derivations, clearances, rounding). Every generated item still needs a staff decision; nothing generated from this ruleset is customer-issuable until the register records both decisions.",
 "sources": [
  "docs/proposals/measurement-to-quotation/survey-and-scope-templates/04-catalogue-record-content.md \u00a72 (rule keys, necessities)",
  "ADR-012 typical 7 ft (2134 mm) wardrobe height (ADR-012 D3)",
  "rate card product inputs and quantity bases (the card in force at BOQ time)",
  "04 \u00a71 'Window seating candidate: window run and sill': a window seat spans the window (its width is the span across the window openings of the tagged wall)",
  "01 \u00a73 and 04 KITCHEN_BASE_FROM_RUNS / KITCHEN_WALL_FROM_RUNS: the base (counter) run is the sum of the tagged walls' runs and continues beneath windows; window spans are deducted from wall units only; the card's single RUN input is the counter length",
  "04 POOJA_UNIT_FROM_WALL: pooja doors take W x H 'from the opening' when a door frame exists, i.e. the pooja room's own door; a niche unit's shutter is not a room door",
  "B1 capture rules: a sensor light records its sensor type and switching; only NEW sensor lights with a real sensor (PIR, MICROWAVE) and sensor switching (SENSOR, BOTH) are sensor provisions",
  "04 KITCHEN_WALL_FROM_RUNS / KITCHEN_LOFT_FROM_CLEARANCE: wall units take the tagged runs less window spans, and the loft run is the wall-unit run; the card's single RUN is therefore evaluated per line on its quantity role (RUN for base units and base shutters, WALL_UNIT_RUN for wall units, lofts and their shutters). The utility card's only measured line is a wall unit. No wall-unit bottom, chimney span or clearance is applied (OI-MTQ-04): every opening whose sill is below the lintel (or the ceiling) is deducted, and an opening without a sill or offset leaves the wall-unit run unresolved."
 ],
 "parameters_note": "No clearance, corner deduction, wastage or rounding beyond the estimator's 0.01 half-up is applied: those are OI-MTQ-04 values, not decided.",
